1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,260
What happened when the snake charmer began to play jazz?
耍蛇人吹起爵士乐时发生了什么？

2
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:19,570
What happened when the snake charmer began to play jazz?
耍蛇人吹起爵士乐时发生了什么？

3
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:28,020
As we had had a long walk through one of the markets of old Delhi,
我们在旧德里的一个市场里走了很久，

4
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:31,790
we stopped at a square to have a rest.
就在一个广场上停下来休息。

5
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:41,330
After a time, we noticed a snake charmer with two large baskets at the other side of the square,
过了一会儿，我们注意到广场另一头有个耍蛇人，身边放着两个大篮子，

6
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:43,610
so we went to have a look at him.
于是我们过去看看。

7
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:46,900
As soon as he saw us,
他一看到我们，

8
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:54,300
he picked up a long pipe which was covered with coins and opened one of the baskets.
就拿起一根镶着硬币的长笛，打开了其中一个篮子。

9
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,100
When he began to play a tune,
当他开始吹奏曲子时，

10
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:02,010
we had our first glimpse of the snake.
我们第一次瞥见了那条蛇。

11
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:09,120
It rose out of the basket and began to follow the movements of the pipe.
它从篮子里探出身子，开始随着笛子的动作舞动。

12
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:14,170
We were very much surprised when the snake charmer
我们非常惊讶的是，耍蛇人

13
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:18,830
suddenly began to play jazz and modern pop songs.
突然吹起爵士乐和现代流行歌曲。

14
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:25,510
The snake, however, continued to 'dance' slowly.
然而那条蛇却继续慢慢地“跳舞”。

15
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:31,830
It obviously could not tell the difference between Indian music and jazz!
它显然分辨不出印度音乐和爵士乐的区别！
